<!-- Website teaching layer for android/architecture/flow.md.
     The original chapter is rendered in full; everything here is added around it.
     stateIn/WhileSubscribed semantics per kotlinx.coroutines API (SharingStarted.WhileSubscribed(stopTimeoutMillis))
     and developer.android.com "StateFlow and SharedFlow"; checked 2026-10-25. -->

<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">A ride-sharing screen shows the user's location three times: on the map, in a header and in a "nearby drivers" list. Each collects the same <code>locationFlow</code>. Battery usage doubles in the next release. The profiler shows three GPS listeners running at once: one per collector, because the flow started its producer again for each one.</p>

A cold `Flow` builder describes work that runs when collected, separately for each collector. That is right for one-off pipelines and wrong for an expensive source that many screens share. A common Android pattern keeps repository queries cold, shares them in the ViewModel with `stateIn`, and collects with lifecycle awareness in the UI. Other sources can already be hot. This chapter follows that pipeline and the policies that decide when upstream work starts and stops.

<!-- @after First Principles :: visual -->
### Cold runs per collector; hot is shared

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-cols" style="--cols:2"><div class="col"><span class="col-title">Cold: <code>flow { }</code></span><div class="node"><strong>Collector A</strong><small>starts its own GPS listener</small></div><div class="node"><strong>Collector B</strong><small>starts another</small></div><div class="node" data-state="warn"><strong>Collector C</strong><small>and another: three producers</small></div></div><div class="col"><span class="col-title">Hot: <code>.stateIn(viewModelScope, …)</code></span><div class="node is-key"><strong>One shared upstream</strong><small>one GPS listener in the ViewModel's scope</small></div><div class="node" data-state="done"><strong>A, B and C</strong><small>read the same latest value</small></div></div></div><figcaption>Sharing is a deliberate step with an owner: the scope you pass to <code>stateIn</code> or <code>shareIn</code>.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Production Example :: animation -->
### What <code>WhileSubscribed(5000)</code> does over a session

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">Upstream work follows subscribers, with a grace period</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="viz-grid" style="--cols:2"><div class="node" data-el="ui"><strong>Screen collectors</strong><small data-text="uiV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="up"><strong>Upstream (Room query)</strong><small data-text="upV">—</small></div></div><div class="node is-key" data-el="state"><strong><code>uiState: StateFlow</code></strong><small data-text="stateV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{"label":"Created","caption":"stateIn is called with WhileSubscribed(5000). Nobody collects yet, so upstream has not started. The StateFlow holds its initial value.","add":["ui","up","state"],"state":{"ui":"ghost","up":"ghost","state":"done"},"text":{"uiV":"none","upV":"not started","stateV":"Loading (initial value)"}},
{"label":"First collector","caption":"The screen starts collecting. The first subscriber starts the shared upstream once; emissions update the StateFlow.","state":{"ui":"active","up":"active"},"text":{"uiV":"1 collector","upV":"running","stateV":"Success(42 users)"}},
{"label":"Rotation","caption":"The old UI stops collecting and the new one starts within a second. The 5-second grace period has not expired, so the subscriber gap does not restart upstream. Room can still re-query for database invalidations.","state":{"ui":"warn"},"text":{"uiV":"0 → 1 collector within 1 s","upV":"still running"}},
{"label":"App in background","caption":"The UI stops collecting (lifecycle below STARTED). After 5 seconds with no subscribers, the upstream is cancelled: no work for an invisible screen. The last value is kept.","state":{"ui":"ghost","up":"ghost"},"text":{"uiV":"0 collectors for 5 s","upV":"cancelled","stateV":"Success(42 users) retained"}},
{"label":"Back to the app","caption":"A new collector arrives: it sees the retained value immediately, and the upstream starts again to refresh it.","state":{"ui":"active","up":"active"},"text":{"uiV":"1 collector","upV":"restarted","stateV":"Success(42 users), then fresh data"}}
]</script><figcaption>The timeout absorbs configuration changes; the stop saves work while nothing is on screen.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @diagram 77fc2dd0a3b7000b -->
### Cold to hot, once, in the ViewModel

<figure class="viz"><div class="viz-flow"><div class="node"><strong>Room DB</strong><small>cold <code>Flow&lt;List&lt;User&gt;&gt;</code></small></div><div class="node"><strong>Domain</strong><small><code>map</code>: keep active users</small></div><div class="node is-key"><strong>ViewModel</strong><small><code>stateIn</code> → hot <code>StateFlow&lt;UiState&gt;</code></small></div><div class="node" data-state="done"><strong>Screen</strong><small><code>collectAsStateWithLifecycle()</code></small></div></div><figcaption>Data layers return cold flows; the ViewModel is the usual place where a stream becomes shared state.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Common Misconceptions :: check -->
**Cold or hot, and where?** Decide before opening each answer.

<details><summary>A DAO method that observes a table.</summary>

Cold `Flow`. Each collector gets its own query that stays live with the table; share it in the ViewModel if several consumers need it.
</details>

<details><summary>A one-time "load profile" network call.</summary>

Neither: a `suspend fun`. Flow is for values over time, not a single result.
</details>

<details><summary>A Fragment collects <code>viewModel.state</code> in <code>lifecycleScope.launch { … }</code>.</summary>

It keeps collecting while stopped and outlives the fragment's views. Use `viewLifecycleOwner.repeatOnLifecycle(STARTED)` (or `collectAsStateWithLifecycle()` in Compose).
</details>

